  "prefLabel": "Bea 602.07 Deed restricted",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 602.07 “Deed restricted” means housing which has a deed rider and is subject to a long-term affordability covenant with a provision for municipal or third-party monitoring which ensures the affordability of the units for a prescribed amount of time and ensures that the occupants of the housing income qualify to live in the housing units.\n\nSource. #14044, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea600.html"
